# Batch files are read CR-delimited by cmd.exe: an LF-only checkout is a
# silently dead launcher. EOL is law here, not preference.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# The unix twin is the mirror image: sh reads the shebang byte-wise, so a
# CRLF checkout is a bad-interpreter death. LF is law here too.
*.sh text eol=lf
